{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115658",
      "title": "Manipulating State & Using Literal Values",
      "lectureOrder": 122,
      "videoOrder": 116,
      "sourceHash": "48031bfeca4d5b6757f05e27936ca0f8bbc1ba1246987b2ff12994176b3ca8da",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "So we got this ServerStatusComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 6.42,
          "en": "but at the moment the status never changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.42,
          "end": 9,
          "en": "Of course, in this demo application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "we are not actually grabbing that server status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "from any real servers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 20.93,
          "en": "but I wanna simulate that it changes every couple of seconds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.94,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "to some random value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "so either to offline, online, or unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 29.94,
          "en": "And to make that work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.94,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "we need to set up an interval that executes some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 37.68,
          "en": "that will change that currentStatus value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.68,
          "end": 39.303,
          "en": "every couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.17,
          "end": 42.873,
          "en": "And we could do that with help of the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 48.98,
          "en": "In there, we can call the built-in setInterval function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.17,
          "end": 51.63,
          "en": "which is provided by JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.63,
          "end": 56.343,
          "en": "so that's of course not Angular or TypeScript specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.54,
          "end": 60.66,
          "en": "And setInterval then takes a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.66,
          "end": 65.19,
          "en": "which it will execute every X amount of milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.19,
          "end": 69.87,
          "en": "And that's the second argument you must pass to setInterval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "the amount of milliseconds it should wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 75.003,
          "en": "until it executes this function again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.93,
          "end": 78.75,
          "en": "And here, let's say we wanna wait five seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.75,
          "end": 82.56,
          "en": "which would be 5000 milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "Now every 5000 milliseconds, every five seconds, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.36,
          "en": "this function will be executed by the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.36,
          "end": 92.673,
          "en": "when the application is running.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 93.96000000000001,
          "end": 95.97,
          "en": "So it's now inside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 95.97,
          "end": 98.10300000000001,
          "en": "where I want to update currentStatus.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.87,
          "end": 104.583,
          "en": "And here I wanna generate a random value with Math.random.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.50999999999999,
          "end": 108.81,
          "en": "And I then simply wanna check if random is smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.81,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "than .5 because Math.random will produce a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 118.7,
          "en": "between zero and one, one excluded, so technically .9999.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 125.94,
          "en": "And if the value that was produced is smaller than .5,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 125.94,
          "end": 129.63,
          "en": "so in 50% of all cases in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 129.63,
          "end": 134.63,
          "en": "I wanna set this currentStatus equal to online, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 142.263,
          "en": "Else if random is smaller than .9,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 146.94,
          "en": "so it's bigger than .5 but smaller than .9,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.94,
          "end": 150.963,
          "en": "in this case, I wanna set the currentStatus to offline,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 152.57999999999998,
          "end": 155.46,
          "en": "and in the remaining 10% of cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 155.46,
          "end": 159.03300000000002,
          "en": "I wanna set currentStatus to unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "Now, one thing you might wanna consider doing here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 166.47,
          "en": "when working with hard-coded values like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 166.47,
          "end": 171.47,
          "en": "is set up a type that only accepts these kinds of values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 174.24,
          "en": "And you can do this in TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 174.24,
          "end": 177.75,
          "en": "by explicitly assigning a type to currentStatus,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 177.75,
          "end": 182.22,
          "en": "which will disable inference for this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 182.22,
          "end": 185.49,
          "en": "because by default it would infer that currentStatus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 185.49,
          "end": 186.903,
          "en": "should be of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 187.74,
          "end": 189.6,
          "en": "But here I wanna be more specific",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 192.21,
          "en": "that it's one of these three strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 192.21,
          "end": 194.52,
          "en": "And you can do that with TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 194.52,
          "end": 197.67000000000002,
          "en": "by disabling the inference for this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 197.67000000000002,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "by explicitly assigning a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "And then you can set up the three string values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "that should be accepted as a union type,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 208.803,
          "en": "so separated by that pipe symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 211.2,
          "end": 214.11,
          "en": "And that tells TypeScript that currentStatus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 214.11,
          "end": 218.613,
          "en": "must be a string that's either online, offline, or unknown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 219.48,
          "end": 221.19,
          "en": "And if I had a typo down there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 221.19,
          "end": 224.01,
          "en": "I would quickly see because I would get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 224.01,
          "end": 226.32,
          "en": "that the type offline written like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 226.32,
          "end": 229.953,
          "en": "is not assignable to my type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 231.69,
          "end": 233.73,
          "en": "And that's why you might wanna do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 233.73,
          "end": 235.5,
          "en": "and be a bit more explicit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 235.5,
          "end": 238.563,
          "en": "because it can help avoid typos like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 240.09,
          "end": 243.51,
          "en": "Well, but with that, we're setting up this interval.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 243.51,
          "end": 246.84,
          "en": "And now if you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 246.84,
          "end": 250.17,
          "en": "you should see that this value should change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 250.17,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "from time to time and it's random.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 256.02,
          "en": "So of course you can't tell how often it will change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 256.02,
          "end": 259.2,
          "en": "to which value, but you see now it's unknown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 259.2,
          "end": 263.22,
          "en": "and eventually it will change again to offline as it seems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 263.22,
          "end": 267.18,
          "en": "at some point it might also be online.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 267.18,
          "end": 268.77,
          "en": "Now it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 268.77,
          "end": 272.19,
          "en": "So that's therefore, working.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 272.19,
          "end": 275.13,
          "en": "But that wasn't even the main thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 275.13,
          "end": 277.14,
          "en": "I wanted to do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 277.14,
          "end": 280.173,
          "en": "though, it is an important step in the right direction.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
